{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:10:config-class"], "search": "from pydantic import BaseModel", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field", "explanation": "Adds the ConfigDict and Field names needed for the v2 model_config and per-field aliases that replace the v1 Config class."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:10:config-class"], "search": "    head_commit_id: str
    repo_name: str
    forced: bool = False

    class Config:
        fields = {
            "head_commit_id": {"alias": "after"},
            "repo_name": {"alias": "repository"},
        }
        allow_population_by_field_name = True", "replace": "    head_commit_id: str = Field(alias="after")
    repo_name: str = Field(alias="repository")
    forced: bool = False

    model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True)", "explanation": "Per the migration guide, the `class Config` namespace is deprecated and `model_config` must be a dict/ConfigDict. The removed `fields` config is replaced by Field(alias=...) on each field, which is the documented approach (use Annotated/Field instead of `fields`). `allow_population_by_field_name` is renamed to `populate_by_name`, so both the alias and the field name are still accepted, matching v1 behavior."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:19:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return GitHubPush.parse_obj(payload)", "replace": "    return GitHubPush.model_validate(payload)", "explanation": "parse_obj() is renamed to model_validate() in Pydantic v2 per the BaseModel method mapping table; behavior is the same for a dict payload."}], "notes": "Three edits cover both findings. The `fields` config was removed in v2 with no direct equivalent, so the aliases moved to Field(alias=...) on head_commit_id and repo_name, which keeps the input names "after" and "repository". `populate_by_name=True` preserves the v1 allow_population_by_field_name behavior. The required-ness of the two aliased fields is unchanged because Field(alias=...) has no default. `ref` and `forced` are untouched. ConfigDict and Field are imported; BaseModel is still used. I did not add pydantic-settings anything since this file has no settings classes. Edits do not overlap and the search strings are copied from the file content provided."}
